  "topic": "signature_help",
  "subtopic": "call_contexts",
  "title": "Class template members",
  "summary": "A member of a class template shows the types the object's class is instantiated with",
  "prose": "`Vector<Point>::at` returns `Point &`, not `T &`, and a call through a\nfunction object shows the parameters of the function type it was declared\nwith. A member template's own parameters stay as it declares them.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "template <typename T>\nstruct Vector {\n    T& at(int index);\n    void assign(int count, const T& value);\n    template <typename U>\n    U convert(U fallback) const;\n};\n\ntemplate <typename... Columns>\nstruct Row {\n    template <typename Tag>\n    void fill(Tag tag, Columns... values);\n    template <typename... Extra>\n    void append(int first, Extra... rest);\n};\n\ntemplate <typename Signature>\nstruct Function;\n\ntemplate <typename Result, typename... Args>\nstruct Function<Result(Args...)> {\n    Result operator()(Args... args) const;\n};\n\nstruct Point {\n    int x;\n    int y;\n};\n\nvoid use(Vector<Point> points, Function<bool(int, double)> callback, Row<int, double> row) {\n    points.at(0);\n    points.assign(3, Point{});\n    points.convert(1.0);\n    callback(1, 2.0);\n    row.fill(0, 1, 2.0);\n    row.append(1, 2);\n}\n",
